# Files Docker must NOT copy into the image ("COPY . ." in the Dockerfile
# respects this list). Two reasons to leave things out: keep the image small
# and fast to build, and, most important, keep secrets out of it.

# Secrets: real env files must never end up inside an image. (The build gets
# the two public Supabase values as build arguments instead, see compose.yaml.)
.env*

# Dependencies are installed fresh inside the image (stage 1 of the Dockerfile).
node_modules

# Build output and caches from your own machine.
.next
out
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control history and tooling that the app does not need to run.
.git
.github
.claude
.scratch
.vercel

# Tests and docs are not part of the running app.
tests
docs
*.md

# Operating-system noise.
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
